==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|ang|gʷʰen}}
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*gunþiz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*gʷʰéntis||killing, blow}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*gʷʰen-||hit, drive}}. Cognate with Old Saxon {{m|osx|gūdea}}, Old High German {{m|goh||gund-}} (in {{m|goh|gundfano||war-flag}}), Old Norse {{m|non|guðr}}, {{m|non|gunnr}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of Latin {{m|la|defendo|defendere}} and {{m|la|offendo|offendere}}, Proto-Slavic {{m|sla-pro|*gъnati-}} (Old Church Slavonic {{m|cu|гънати}}, Russian {{m|ru|гнать}}), Avestan {{m|ae|𐬘𐬀𐬌𐬥𐬙𐬌||to kill|tr=jainti}}, Sanskrit {{m|sa|हन्ति|tr=hanti||to slay}}, Lithuanian {{m|lt|giñti}} as well as Old Irish {{m|sga|gonaid}}.

